<td id="A2.T4.3.1.4.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">1.000</td>
<td id="A2.T4.3.1.4.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">0.866</td>
<td id="A2.T4.3.1.4.7" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">0.894</td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T4.3.1.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T4.3.1.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb">Final SSR</td>
<td id="A2.T4.3.1.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">0.489</td>
<td id="A2.T4.3.1.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">0.274</td>
<td id="A2.T4.3.1.5.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">0.866</td>
<td id="A2.T4.3.1.5.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">1.000</td>
<td id="A2.T4.3.1.5.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">0.903</td></tr>
</table>
</span></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A2.T4.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table A4</span>: </span><span id="A2.T4.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
<span id="A2.T4.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">CAMAP Analysis</span>.
We compute the average CAMAP correlation between different types of tokens:
Animal-related tokens, Object-related tokens, Initial SSR-related tokens, Final SSR-related tokens, and Other tokens.
The fine-tuned model shows a stronger correlation between the <math id="A2.T4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\text{\emph{initial SSR}}\rangle\text{\emph{-to-}}\langle\text{\emph{animal}}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.110em" minsize="1.110em" stretchy="true">⟨</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"><em class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">initial SSR</em></mtext><mo maxsize="1.110em" minsize="1.110em" stretchy="true">⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"><em class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">-to-</em></mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.110em" minsize="1.110em" stretchy="true">⟨</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"><em class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">animal</em></mtext><mo maxsize="1.110em" minsize="1.110em" stretchy="true">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\text{\emph{initial SSR}}\rangle\text{\emph{-to-}}\langle\text{\emph{animal}}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.T4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\text{\emph{final SSR}}\rangle\text{\emph{-to-}}\langle\text{\emph{animal}}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.110em" minsize="1.110em" stretchy="true">⟨</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"><em class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">final SSR</em></mtext><mo maxsize="1.110em" minsize="1.110em" stretchy="true">⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"><em class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">-to-</em></mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.110em" minsize="1.110em" stretchy="true">⟨</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"><em class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">animal</em></mtext><mo maxsize="1.110em" minsize="1.110em" stretchy="true">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\text{\emph{final SSR}}\rangle\text{\emph{-to-}}\langle\text{\emph{animal}}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> pairs, indicating better capturing of the spatial relationships specified in the DSR prompts.
</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A2.F8" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2602.22745v1/pdf_loss_curve.png" id="A2.F8.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_portrait" style="aspect-ratio:476/673;" width="476" height="673" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A2.F8.12" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure A8</span>: </span><span id="A2.F8.13" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Training curves<span id="A2.F8.13.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> of <math id="A2.F8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{DPO}}+\lambda_{\text{ZO}}\mathcal{L}_{\text{ZO}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>DPO</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mtext>ZO</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>ZO</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{DPO}}+\lambda_{\text{ZO}}\mathcal{L}_{\text{ZO}}</annotation></semantics></math> (black) and <math id="A2.F8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{DPO}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>DPO</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{DPO}}</annotation></semantics></math> (<span id="A2.F8.13.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">blue</span>).
With only <math id="A2.F8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{DPO}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>DPO</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{DPO}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the training exhibits <span id="A2.F8.13.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">likelihood displacement</span>:
the winner-side implicit reward <span id="A2.F8.13.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">score_pos</span> drops catastrophically and the loser-side reward <span id="A2.F8.13.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">score_neg</span> drops even further,
raising up the <span id="A2.F8.13.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">score_margin</span> in an incorrect way.
In contrast, the existence of <math id="A2.F8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{ZO}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>ZO</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{ZO}}</annotation></semantics></math> keeps <span id="A2.F8.13.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">score_pos</span> at slight growth and <span id="A2.F8.13.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">score_neg</span> at slight drop,
giving a healthier growing of <span id="A2.F8.13.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">score_margin</span>.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Ablations on the loss setting with training curves.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This is an extension of <a href="#S3.F3" title="In 3.4 DPO with Zeroth-Order Regularization ‣ 3 Method ‣ SpatialAlign: Aligning Dynamic Spatial Relationships in Video Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figures</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> and <a href="#S4.SS3" title="4.3 Ablations ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ SpatialAlign: Aligning Dynamic Spatial Relationships in Video Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a> in the main paper.
We show the training curves of DPO loss <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{DPO}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>DPO</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{DPO}}</annotation></semantics></math> and with the regularization losses <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{ZO}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>ZO</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{ZO}}</annotation></semantics></math> in <a href="#A2.F8" title="In Analysis of Internal Changes in Text-to-Latent Attention. ‣ Appendix A2 Additional Analysis ‣ SpatialAlign: Aligning Dynamic Spatial Relationships in Video Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A8</span></a>.
It can be observed that with only DPO loss, the training is unstable and the loss fluctuates heavily.
With our zeroth-order regularization, the DPO process exhibits more stable training.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.F9" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A2.F9.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2602.22745v1/auc_method.svg" id="A2.F9.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/476;" width="476" height="476"></object>
