This is an extended version of <a href="#S4.T3" title="In Qualitative Results. ‣ 4.2 Main Results ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ SpatialAlign: Aligning Dynamic Spatial Relationships in Video Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> in the main paper, showing the correctness curves of various ablations.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A3 </span>Correctness Curves of Ablation Studies</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We show the correctness curves of the ablation studies discussed in <a href="#S4.SS3" title="4.3 Ablations ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ SpatialAlign: Aligning Dynamic Spatial Relationships in Video Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a> to convey additional information beyond the singular values provided in the main paper.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#A2.F9.sf1" title="In Figure A9 ‣ Ablations on the loss setting with training curves. ‣ Appendix A2 Additional Analysis ‣ SpatialAlign: Aligning Dynamic Spatial Relationships in Video Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figures</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9(a)</span></a> and <a href="#A2.F9.sf2" title="Figure 9(b) ‣ Figure A9 ‣ Ablations on the loss setting with training curves. ‣ Appendix A2 Additional Analysis ‣ SpatialAlign: Aligning Dynamic Spatial Relationships in Video Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9(b)</span></a> show the ablation under different training losses.
Our setting of doing DPO with <math id="A3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\text{train}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mtext>train</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\text{train}}</annotation></semantics></math> shows a clear advantage over SFT/DPO w/o <math id="A3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\text{train}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mtext>train</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\text{train}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
As for the choice of regularization loss, our <math id="A3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{ZO}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>ZO</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{ZO}}</annotation></semantics></math> performs better than <math id="A3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{SFT}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>SFT</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{SFT}}</annotation></semantics></math> as the training progresses to 2400 steps.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#A2.F9.sf4" title="In Figure A9 ‣ Ablations on the loss setting with training curves. ‣ Appendix A2 Additional Analysis ‣ SpatialAlign: Aligning Dynamic Spatial Relationships in Video Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9(d)</span></a> shows the ablation on different <math id="A3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\text{train}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mtext>train</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\text{train}}</annotation></semantics></math> for splitting the winner/loser training samples.
As <math id="A3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\text{train}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mtext>train</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\text{train}}</annotation></semantics></math> goes from 0.6 to 0.8, an overall shift is witnessed across all <math id="A3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\text{test}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mtext>test</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\text{test}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
This shows that our <span id="A3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">DSR-Score</span> can serve as a stable and progressive optimization signal.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#A2.F9.sf5" title="In Figure A9 ‣ Ablations on the loss setting with training curves. ‣ Appendix A2 Additional Analysis ‣ SpatialAlign: Aligning Dynamic Spatial Relationships in Video Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figures</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9(e)</span></a> and <a href="#A2.F9.sf3" title="Figure 9(c) ‣ Figure A9 ‣ Ablations on the loss setting with training curves. ‣ Appendix A2 Additional Analysis ‣ SpatialAlign: Aligning Dynamic Spatial Relationships in Video Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9(c)</span></a>
show the ablation using different reward systems.
With only endpoint values, fine-tuning is unable to reach the same level of performance as using the full <span id="A3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">DSR-Score</span>. Compared to VLM-based evaluation, our <span id="A3.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">DSR-Score</span> gives a much better performance,
suggesting that our metric is more reliable in terms of providing an optimization signal for fine-tuning.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#A2.F9.sf6" title="In Figure A9 ‣ Ablations on the loss setting with training curves. ‣ Appendix A2 Additional Analysis ‣ SpatialAlign: Aligning Dynamic Spatial Relationships in Video Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9(f)</span></a> shows the result of testing on different prompt structures, despite only fine-tuning our model with a specific prompt structure.
For all three types of alternative prompts, the fine-tuned model performs better than the baseline.
This suggests that the fine-tuned model has acquired some semantic knowledge about spatial relationships, rather than simply overfitting to the training prompts.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A4 </span>Theoretical Analysis of the Regularization Term <math id="A4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{ZO}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>ZO</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{ZO}}</annotation></semantics></math></h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The original DPO loss is</p>
<table id="A4.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{DPO}}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>DPO</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{DPO}}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\mathbb{E}_{(p,x^{w},x^{l},t)}\Big[\log\sigma\Big(\beta\big(" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>w</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\mathbb{E}_{(p,x^{w},x^{l},t)}\Big[\log\sigma\Big(\beta\big(</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(\|\epsilon^{w}-\epsilon_{\theta}(x_{t}^{w},t)\|_{2}^{2}-\|\epsilon^{w}-\epsilon_{\mathrm{ref}}(x_{t}^{w},t)\|_{2}^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>w</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>w</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(\|\epsilon^{w}-\epsilon_{\theta}(x_{t}^{w},t)\|_{2}^{2}-\|\epsilon^{w}-\epsilon_{\mathrm{ref}}(x_{t}^{w},t)\|_{2}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle-(\|\epsilon^{l}-\epsilon_{\theta}(x_{t}^{l},t)\|_{2}^{2}-\|\epsilon^{l}-\epsilon_{\mathrm{ref}}(x_{t}^{l},t)\|_{2}^{2})\big)\Big)\Big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-(\|\epsilon^{l}-\epsilon_{\theta}(x_{t}^{l},t)\|_{2}^{2}-\|\epsilon^{l}-\epsilon_{\mathrm{ref}}(x_{t}^{l},t)\|_{2}^{2})\big)\Big)\Big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Denote</p>
<table id="A4.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A_{\theta}^{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A_{\theta}^{w}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\|\epsilon^{w}-\epsilon_{\theta}(x_{t}^{w},t)\|_{2}^{2}-\|\epsilon^{w}-\epsilon_{\mathrm{ref}}(x_{t}^{w},t)\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>w</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>w</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\|\epsilon^{w}-\epsilon_{\theta}(x_{t}^{w},t)\|_{2}^{2}-\|\epsilon^{w}-\epsilon_{\mathrm{ref}}(x_{t}^{w},t)\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A_{\theta}^{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A_{\theta}^{l}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\|\epsilon^{l}-\epsilon_{\theta}(x_{t}^{l},t)\|_{2}^{2}-\|\epsilon^{l}-\epsilon_{\mathrm{ref}}(x_{t}^{l},t)\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\|\epsilon^{l}-\epsilon_{\theta}(x_{t}^{l},t)\|_{2}^{2}-\|\epsilon^{l}-\epsilon_{\mathrm{ref}}(x_{t}^{l},t)\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle z</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\beta\big(A_{\theta}^{w}-A_{\theta}^{l}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\beta\big(A_{\theta}^{w}-A_{\theta}^{l}\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{DPO}}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>DPO</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{DPO}}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\mathbb{E}\Big[\log\sigma(z)\Big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\mathbb{E}\Big[\log\sigma(z)\Big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">then the gradient of the DPO loss is</p>
<table id="A4.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{DPO}}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>DPO</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{DPO}}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\mathbb{E}\Big[(1-\sigma(z))\,\nabla_{\theta}z\Big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\mathbb{E}\Big[(1-\sigma(z))\,\nabla_{\theta}z\Big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">where the gradient <math id="A4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}z</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="A4.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta}z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta}z</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\beta\big(\nabla_{\theta}A_{\theta}^{w}-\nabla_{\theta}A_{\theta}^{l}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\beta\big(\nabla_{\theta}A_{\theta}^{w}-\nabla_{\theta}A_{\theta}^{l}\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta}A_{\theta}^{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta}A_{\theta}^{w}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=2\,(\nabla_{\theta}\epsilon_{\theta}(x_{t}^{w},t))^{\top}\big(\epsilon_{\theta}(x_{t}^{w},t)-\epsilon^{w}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>w</mi></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=2\,(\nabla_{\theta}\epsilon_{\theta}(x_{t}^{w},t))^{\top}\big(\epsilon_{\theta}(x_{t}^{w},t)-\epsilon^{w}\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta}A_{\theta}^{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta}A_{\theta}^{l}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=2\,(\nabla_{\theta}\epsilon_{\theta}(x_{t}^{l},t))^{\top}\big(\epsilon_{\theta}(x_{t}^{l},t)-\epsilon^{l}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=2\,(\nabla_{\theta}\epsilon_{\theta}(x_{t}^{l},t))^{\top}\big(\epsilon_{\theta}(x_{t}^{l},t)-\epsilon^{l}\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Denote</p>
<table id="A4.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle J^{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>J</mi><mi>w</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle J^{w}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\nabla_{\theta}\epsilon_{\theta}(x_{t}^{w},t),\quad J^{l}=\nabla_{\theta}\epsilon_{\theta}(x_{t}^{l},t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>J</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\nabla_{\theta}\epsilon_{\theta}(x_{t}^{w},t),\quad J^{l}=\nabla_{\theta}\epsilon_{\theta}(x_{t}^{l},t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\delta^{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>δ</mi><mi>w</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\delta^{w}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\delta_{\theta}(x_{t}^{w},t)=\epsilon_{\theta}(x_{t}^{w},t)-\epsilon_{ref}(x_{t}^{w},t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\delta_{\theta}(x_{t}^{w},t)=\epsilon_{\theta}(x_{t}^{w},t)-\epsilon_{ref}(x_{t}^{w},t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\delta^{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>δ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\delta^{l}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\delta_{\theta}(x_{t}^{l},t)=\epsilon_{\theta}(x_{t}^{l},t)-\epsilon_{ref}(x_{t}^{l},t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\delta_{\theta}(x_{t}^{l},t)=\epsilon_{\theta}(x_{t}^{l},t)-\epsilon_{ref}(x_{t}^{l},t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p5.1" class="ltx_p">At the neighborhood of <math id="A4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{ref}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{ref}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="A4.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\!\left[\epsilon-\epsilon_{\mathrm{ref}}(x_{t},t)\ \right]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\!\left[\epsilon-\epsilon_{\mathrm{ref}}(x_{t},t)\ \right]=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p5.2" class="ltx_p">then</p>
<table id="A4.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\delta^{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>δ</mi><mi>w</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\delta^{w}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\approx\epsilon_{\theta}(x_{t}^{w},t)-\epsilon^{w},\quad\delta^{l}\approx\epsilon_{\theta}(x_{t}^{l},t)-\epsilon^{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>w</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>δ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\approx\epsilon_{\theta}(x_{t}^{w},t)-\epsilon^{w},\quad\delta^{l}\approx\epsilon_{\theta}(x_{t}^{l},t)-\epsilon^{l}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p5.3" class="ltx_p">and the gradient can be written as</p>
<table id="A4.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta}z=\beta\big(\nabla_{\theta}A_{\theta}^{w}-\nabla_{\theta}A_{\theta}^{l}\big)\approx 2\beta\Big((J^{w})^{\top}\delta^{w}-(J^{l})^{\top}\delta^{l}\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>J</mi><mi>w</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mi>w</mi></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>J</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta}z=\beta\big(\nabla_{\theta}A_{\theta}^{w}-\nabla_{\theta}A_{\theta}^{l}\big)\approx 2\beta\Big((J^{w})^{\top}\delta^{w}-(J^{l})^{\top}\delta^{l}\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p6.1" class="ltx_p">The regularization loss is</p>
<table id="A4.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{ZO}}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>ZO</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{ZO}}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex3.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{(p,x^{w},x^{l},t)}\Big[\|\epsilon_{\theta}(x_{t}^{w},t)-\epsilon_{\mathrm{ref}}(x_{t}^{w},t)\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>w</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{(p,x^{w},x^{l},t)}\Big[\|\epsilon_{\theta}(x_{t}^{w},t)-\epsilon_{\mathrm{ref}}(x_{t}^{w},t)\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E16.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle+\|\epsilon_{\theta}(x_{t}^{l},t)-\epsilon_{\mathrm{ref}}(x_{t}^{l},t)\|_{2}^{2}\Big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">+</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\|\epsilon_{\theta}(x_{t}^{l},t)-\epsilon_{\mathrm{ref}}(x_{t}^{l},t)\|_{2}^{2}\Big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p6.2" class="ltx_p">its gradient is</p>
<table id="A4.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{ZO}}=2\,\mathbb{E}\Big[(\nabla_{\theta}\epsilon_{\theta}(x_{t}^{w},t))^{\top}\big(\epsilon_{\theta}(x_{t}^{w},t)-\epsilon_{\mathrm{ref}}(x_{t}^{w},t)\big)+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>ZO</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{ZO}}=2\,\mathbb{E}\Big[(\nabla_{\theta}\epsilon_{\theta}(x_{t}^{w},t))^{\top}\big(\epsilon_{\theta}(x_{t}^{w},t)-\epsilon_{\mathrm{ref}}(x_{t}^{w},t)\big)+</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E17.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle(\nabla_{\theta}\epsilon_{\theta}(x_{t}^{l},t))^{\top}\big(\epsilon_{\theta}(x_{t}^{l},t)-\epsilon_{\mathrm{ref}}(x_{t}^{l},t)\big)\Big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(\nabla_{\theta}\epsilon_{\theta}(x_{t}^{l},t))^{\top}\big(\epsilon_{\theta}(x_{t}^{l},t)-\epsilon_{\mathrm{ref}}(x_{t}^{l},t)\big)\Big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p7.1" class="ltx_p">With <math id="A4.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J^{w},J^{l},\delta^{w},\delta^{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>J</mi><mi>w</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>J</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mi>w</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J^{w},J^{l},\delta^{w},\delta^{l}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A4.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{ZO}}=2\,\mathbb{E}\Big[(J^{w})^{\top}\delta^{w}+(J^{l})^{\top}\delta^{l}\Big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>ZO</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>J</mi><mi>w</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mi>w</mi></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>J</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{ZO}}=2\,\mathbb{E}\Big[(J^{w})^{\top}\delta^{w}+(J^{l})^{\top}\delta^{l}\Big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p8.1" class="ltx_p">Denote</p>
<table id="A4.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\delta^{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>δ</mi><mi>S</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\delta^{S}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\big(\delta^{w}+\delta^{l}\big),\quad\delta^{D}=\frac{1}{2}\big(\delta^{w}-\delta^{l}\big)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>δ</mi><mi>w</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>δ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>δ</mi><mi>w</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\big(\delta^{w}+\delta^{l}\big),\quad\delta^{D}=\frac{1}{2}\big(\delta^{w}-\delta^{l}\big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle J^{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>J</mi><mi>S</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle J^{S}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\big(J^{w}+J^{l}\big),\quad J^{D}=\frac{1}{2}\big(J^{w}-J^{l}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>J</mi><mi>w</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>J</mi><mi>l</mi></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>J</mi><mi>D</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>J</mi><mi>w</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>J</mi><mi>l</mi></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\big(J^{w}+J^{l}\big),\quad J^{D}=\frac{1}{2}\big(J^{w}-J^{l}\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p9.1" class="ltx_p">Then the two gradient can be written as</p>
<table id="A4.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta}z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta}z</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\approx 2\beta\Big((J^{w})^{\top}\delta^{w}-(J^{l})^{\top}\delta^{l}\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>J</mi><mi>w</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mi>w</mi></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>J</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\approx 2\beta\Big((J^{w})^{\top}\delta^{w}-(J^{l})^{\top}\delta^{l}\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=4\beta\Big((J^{S})^{\top}\delta^{D}+(J^{D})^{\top}\delta^{S}\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>J</mi><mi>S</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>J</mi><mi>D</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mi>S</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=4\beta\Big((J^{S})^{\top}\delta^{D}+(J^{D})^{\top}\delta^{S}\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{ZO}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>ZO</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{ZO}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=2\mathbb{E}\Big[(J^{w})^{\top}\delta^{w}+(J^{l})^{\top}\delta^{l}\Big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>J</mi><mi>w</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mi>w</mi></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>J</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=2\mathbb{E}\Big[(J^{w})^{\top}\delta^{w}+(J^{l})^{\top}\delta^{l}\Big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=4\mathbb{E}\Big[(J^{S})^{\top}\delta^{S}+(J^{D})^{\top}\delta^{D}\Big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>J</mi><mi>S</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mi>S</mi></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>J</mi><mi>D</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=4\mathbb{E}\Big[(J^{S})^{\top}\delta^{S}+(J^{D})^{\top}\delta^{D}\Big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p10.1" class="ltx_p">Given the same prompt and the same denoising timestep <math id="A4.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, the two samples <math id="A4.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>w</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{w}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{l}</annotation></semantics></math> are located within a neighborhood, making <math id="A4.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J^{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>J</mi><mi>w</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J^{w}</annotation></semantics></math> close to <math id="A4.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J^{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>J</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J^{l}</annotation></semantics></math> in terms of norm. This is even consolidated under the low-rank adaption (LoRA) setting of optimization. Therefore, the common component <math id="A4.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J^{S}=\frac{1}{2}\big(J^{w}+J^{l}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>J</mi><mi>S</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>J</mi><mi>w</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>J</mi><mi>l</mi></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J^{S}=\frac{1}{2}\big(J^{w}+J^{l}\big)</annotation></semantics></math> should be dominant over <math id="A4.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J^{D}=\frac{1}{2}\big(J^{w}-J^{l}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>J</mi><mi>D</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>J</mi><mi>w</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>J</mi><mi>l</mi></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J^{D}=\frac{1}{2}\big(J^{w}-J^{l}\big)</annotation></semantics></math> in terms of norm. 
<br class="ltx_break"></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p11.1" class="ltx_p">In the gradient of DPO <math id="A4.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}z</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J^{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>J</mi><mi>s</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J^{s}</annotation></semantics></math> amplifies the difference part <math id="A4.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>δ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta^{D}</annotation></semantics></math>, leading to a shift towards <math id="A4.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>w</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{w}</annotation></semantics></math>. However, the common part <math id="A4.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta^{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>δ</mi><mi>S</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta^{S}</annotation></semantics></math> is not amplified at the same level, since <math id="A4.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>J</mi><mi>D</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J^{D}</annotation></semantics></math> is rather small. This undermines the foundation level of alignment to the prompt. In fact, when we want to shift the model distribution towards the preferred samples, an implicit assumption is that the basic level of alignment to both preferred and unwanted samples should be maintained. 
<br class="ltx_break"></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p12.1" class="ltx_p">In the gradient of <math id="A4.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{ZO}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>ZO</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{ZO}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the common part <math id="A4.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta^{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>δ</mi><mi>S</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta^{S}</annotation></semantics></math> is reserved by the dominant component <math id="A4.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J^{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>J</mi><mi>S</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J^{S}</annotation></semantics></math>, <span id="A4.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">counteracting</span> the risk of “losing the common ground” induced in <math id="A4.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}z</annotation></semantics></math>, which helps to maintain the stability at a coefficient <math id="A4.p12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{ZO}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{ZO}</annotation></semantics></math>. 
<br class="ltx_break"></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p13.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A4.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{ZO}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>ZO</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{ZO}}</annotation></semantics></math> only constrains the win part <math id="A4.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon^{w}_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon^{w}_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, then the gradient will be</p>
<table id="A4.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(J^{S})^{\top}\delta^{S}+(J^{S})^{\top}\delta^{D}+(J^{D})^{\top}\delta^{S}+(J^{D})^{\top}\delta^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>J</mi><mi>S</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mi>S</mi></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>J</mi><mi>S</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>J</mi><mi>D</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mi>S</mi></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>J</mi><mi>D</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(J^{S})^{\top}\delta^{S}+(J^{S})^{\top}\delta^{D}+(J^{D})^{\top}\delta^{S}+(J^{D})^{\top}\delta^{D}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p13.2" class="ltx_p">which contains some part of <math id="A4.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}z</annotation></semantics></math> and the alleviation is not as effective.</p>
</div>
</section>
